---
description: Check the current ARC task declarations before repository edits
alwaysApply: true
---

Before changing files for a declared task, read `.arc/bundle.json` and `.arc/task.json` and run `npm run arc:check` from the consumer root.

Keep the existing project rules, task approval, and tool permissions. Exit 0 covers declaration consistency only. Exit 1 requires resolving the reported declaration or JSON validation rejection; exit 2 means an input could not be read or the CLI/tool check did not complete. Do not expand the allowed scope or remove a reviewer merely to make a check pass.

Rerun after an approved task or role change. Record the observed result. If commands cannot be run, say that the check was not run. This rule provides model context; it is not a hook, sandbox, or authorization system.
